ng>$3.50</strong></p>\n    <button type=\"button\" data-action=\"Food details screen for a butter croissant, priced at $3.50\">Details</button>\n    <button type=\"button\" class=\"add\" data-name=\"Butter Croissant\" data-price=\"3.50\">Add to order</button>\n  </article>\n\n  <article>\n    <h2>Your order <small id=\"count\">0 items</small></h2>\n    <p id=\"summary\">Add something delicious to get started.</p>\n    <p>Subtotal: <strong id=\"total\">$0.00</strong></p>\n    <button type=\"button\" data-action=\"Checkout screen for a coffee shop order with selected items\">Checkout</button>\n    <button type=\"button\" data-action=\"Edit order screen with selected drinks and quantity controls\">Edit order</button>\n    <button type=\"button\" data-action=\"Order customization screen for adding drink modifiers\">Customize</button>\n  </article>\n</main>\n\n<script>\n  const items = [];\n  const money = n => \"$\" + n.toFixed(2);\n  document.querySelectorAll(\".add\").forEach(button => button.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n    items.push({ name: button.dataset.name, price: Number(button.dataset.price) });\n    document.getElementById(\"count\").textContent = `${items.length} ${items.length === 1 ? \"item\" : \"items\"}`;\n    document.getElementById(\"summary\").textContent = items.map(item => item.name).join(\", \");\n    document.getElementById(\"total\").textContent = money(items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0));\n  }));\n</script>"}

